● Confirmed Milo's API usage is correct — the only failure was the expected "no
  residual df" dispersion error, the exact same root cause as the DESeq2 bug (1
  sample per condition, 0 replicates). scCODA worked fine since it's Bayesian,
  not relying on residual-df dispersion estimation. My planned
  tryCatch-per-contrast structure already handles this gracefully. Now
  finalizing run_milo(), run_gsea(), and make_downstream_summary() in
