  ⎿  Added 61 lines, removed 1 line
      114  - **Two count layers.** `normalize()` stores raw integer count
           s in `adata.layers["counts"]` before `normalize_total`/`log1p`
           , then freezes log-norm in `adata.raw`. `downstream.R` reads `
           layers["counts"]` → assay `"counts"` (for DESeq2) and `adata.X
           ` → assay `"X"` (for LIANA/NMF). Removing the `counts` layer h
           ard-fails Stage 5a.
      115  - **`cell_type` is a fixed contract column.** Always written b
           y `cluster_and_annotate()` (CellTypist labels if available, el
           se leiden IDs as strings). `downstream.R` hardcodes `ctype_col
            <- "cell_type"`.
      116  - **`sample` is the universal batch key.** Set at load time; u
           sed for HVG batch-awareness and as the Harmony key.
      117 -- **Condition column is auto-detected in R.** `detect_conditio
          -n_col()` picks the first `obs` column not in `PIPELINE_COLS` w
          -ith 2–10 distinct values. **Any new pipeline-generated `obs` c
          -olumn with 2–10 distinct values must be added to `PIPELINE_COL
          -S`, or it can silently become the DEG grouping variable instea
          -d of the real condition** — this actually happened when `scDbl
          -Finder_class` (singlet/doublet) was added without updating the
          - list, and Stage 5 silently ran DESeq2/GSEA on "singlet vs dou
          -blet" instead of the real experimental condition. `PIPELINE_CO
          -LS` must stay in sync with every `obs` column `scanpy_analysis
          -.py` writes (QC metrics, `outlier`/`mt_outlier`, doublet colum
          -ns).                                                          
      117 +- **Condition column is auto-detected, independently, in both 
          +R and Python.** `downstream.R`'s `detect_condition_col()`/`PIP
          +ELINE_COLS` and `differential_abundance.py`'s port of the same
          + logic both pick the first `obs` column not in their (separate
          +ly maintained) `PIPELINE_COLS` list with 2–10 distinct values.
          + **Any new pipeline-generated `obs` column with 2–10 distinct 
          +values must be added to BOTH copies of `PIPELINE_COLS`, or it 
          +can silently become the DEG/DA grouping variable instead of th
          +e real condition** — this actually happened once in R when `sc
          +DblFinder_class` (singlet/doublet) was added without updating 
          +the list, and Stage 5 silently ran DESeq2/GSEA on "singlet vs 
          +doublet" instead of the real experimental condition. Both list
          +s must stay in sync with every `obs` column `scanpy_analysis.p
          +y` writes (QC metrics, `outlier`/`mt_outlier`, doublet columns
          +).                                                            
      118  - **`sample_metadata.tsv` `sample` column must exactly match `
           SAMPLES=()` in config.** `merge_metadata()` errors on any miss
           ing sample.
      119  
      120  ---
      121  
      122 +## Multi-condition analysis (`CONTROL_CONDITION`)             
      123 +                                                              
      124 +`CONTROL_CONDITION` names the reference/baseline level of the 
          +auto-detected                                                 
      125 +condition column. It's consumed identically by Stage 4b (scCOD
          +A), Stage 5a                                                  
      126 +(DESeq2), and Stage 5f (Milo):                                
      127 +                                                              
      128 +- **Required if the condition column has more than 2 levels.**
          + Without it,                                                  
      129 +  DESeq2's `results()` (and edgeR inside Milo's `testNhoods()`
          +) would otherwise                                             
      130 +  silently return only the last-vs-first-alphabetical coeffici
          +ent — e.g. a                                                  
      131 +  4-level `condition` column with values `cocktail`/`control`/
          +`plastic5`/                                                   
      132 +  `plastic50` would silently compare `plastic50 vs cocktail`, 
          +never touching                                                
      133 +  the real control. `differential_abundance.py` and `downstrea
          +m.R` each                                                     
      134 +  independently enforce this and abort (exit 1) with an error 
          +naming the                                                    
      135 +  detected levels if it's unset — whichever stage runs first (
          +Stage 4b runs                                                 
      136 +  before Stage 5) surfaces the error via `run_pipeline.sh`'s `
          +set -o pipefail`.                                             
      137 +- **Optional for exactly 2 levels** — only affects which level
          + fold-changes                                                 
      138 +  are computed against; leaving it unset keeps prior behavior 
          +unchanged (an                                                 
      139 +  arbitrary but deterministic reference).                     
      140 +- **Every non-control level gets its own vs-control contrast**
          +, named                                                       
      141 +  `<level>_vs_<CONTROL_CONDITION>` (sanitized like cell-type n
          +ames,                                                         
      142 +  `[^A-Za-z0-9_]` → `_`): `DEG_<celltype>__<level>_vs_<control
          +>.tsv`,                                                       
      143 +  `GSEA_<celltype>__<level>_vs_<control>.tsv`,                
      144 +  `milo_DA_<level>_vs_<control>.tsv`. GSEA runs once per (cell
          + type × contrast)                                             
      145 +  — accepted ~(n_levels−1)× runtime cost over the 2-level case
          +.                                                             
      146 +- **Figure-splitting rule**: when a summary figure can't legib
          +ly hold                                                       
      147 +  cell-type × contrast × collection on one static page, it spl
          +its into one                                                  
      148 +  file per non-control level — same rationale as `umap_overvie
          +w.pdf`'s split                                                
      149 +  into `umap_leiden.pdf`/`umap_cell_type.pdf` to avoid legend 
          +overflow.                                                     
      150 +  `04_deg_summary__<level>_vs_<control>.pdf`,                 
      151 +  `08_gsea_summary__<level>_vs_<control>.pdf`,                
      152 +  `09_milo_beeswarm__<level>_vs_<control>.pdf` each split this
          + way;                                                         
      153 +  `05_volcano_top_celltype.pdf` stays a single file (global be
          +st                                                            
      154 +  cell_type × contrast pair by DEG count). **scCODA is the one
          + exception** —                                                
      155 +  its whole point is one joint model across every condition le
          +vel at once                                                   
      156 +  (`C(condition, Treatment('<control>'))` in a single `sample_
          +hmc()` fit), so                                               
      157 +  `sccoda_effects.tsv`/`10_sccoda_effects.pdf` stay singular, 
          +faceted                                                       
      158 +  internally by level instead.                                
      159 +- **Milo needs replicated samples per condition just like DESe
          +q2 does** —                                                   
      160 +  `testNhoods()` calls edgeR's `estimateDisp()` internally, wh
          +ich needs                                                     
      161 +  residual degrees of freedom the same way DESeq2 does. With 1
          + sample per                                                   
      162 +  condition, every contrast logs "No residual df: setting disp
          +ersion to NA"                                                 
      163 +  and 0 `milo_DA_*.tsv` tables get written — not a bug, the sa
          +me                                                            
      164 +  experimental-design limit as DESeq2, just surfacing a second
          + time. scCODA                                                 
      165 +  (Bayesian) can still produce output in this case, just with 
          +limited                                                       
      166 +  statistical confidence.                                     
      167 +- **Stage 4b (`differential_abundance.py`, scCODA)** reads onl
          +y                                                             
      168 +  `obs_metadata.csv` (already written by Stage 2-4) — independ
          +ent of Stage 5,                                               
      169 +  runs right after it, doesn't wait on `downstream.R`. `sccoda
          +`'s reference                                                 
      170 +  cell type is auto-selected (its own dispersion-based heurist
          +ic) — no                                                      
      171 +  separate config var for it.                                 
      172 +- **Stage 5f (Milo, in `downstream.R`)** needs PCA coordinates
          +, so it only                                                  
      173 +  runs on the `annotated.h5ad`/zellkonverter path — the `count
          +s_matrix.csv`                                                 
      174 +  fallback near the top of `downstream.R` never builds an `sce
          +` object, so                                                  
      175 +  Milo is skipped with a log line in that case. Builds its kNN
          + graph on                                                     
      176 +  `reducedDim(sce, "X_pca_harmony")` if present else `"X_pca"`
          + (mirrors                                                     
      177 +  `scanpy_analysis.py`'s own `use_rep` fallback) — both land i
          +n the h5ad via                                                
      178 +  `adata.obsm` automatically, no extra Python-side export need
          +ed.                                                           
      179 +                                                              
      180 +---                                                           
