● All three implementation items are complete and validated end-to-end on real
  data. Summary of what was built and found:

  1. Multi-condition analysis (CONTROL_CONDITION)
  - New config var in config.sh/my_project.sh. Hard-required when the condition
  column has >2 levels (your choice); optional for exactly 2.
  - downstream.R's DESeq2 stage now runs one contrast per non-control level
  (DEG_<celltype>__<level>_vs_<control>.tsv), instead of DESeq2's default silent
  alphabetical-reference pick. GSEA mirrors this per-contrast. Figures split
  per-level (04_deg_summary__*, 08_gsea_summary__*) following the same
  overflow-avoidance convention as umap_overview.pdf's earlier split.

  2. scCODA (Stage 4b) + Milo (Stage 5f)
  - New differential_abundance.py runs scCODA right after Stage 2-4, independent
  of Stage 5 — writes sccoda_effects.tsv + 10_sccoda_effects.pdf.
  - New run_milo() in downstream.R — kNN-neighborhood differential abundance,
  one milo_DA_<level>_vs_<control>.tsv + beeswarm plot per contrast.
  - Chose standalone sccoda over pertpy's reimplementation after real testing
  showed pertpy would upgrade anndata past the pipeline's hard <0.11 pin
  (breaking Stage 5's h5ad reading); sccoda needed tf-keras added alongside it
  to fix a broken import, confirmed no conflicts.

  3. Perturbation modeling on plastics_test: answered inline — technically
  fittable (enough cells), but scientifically unreliable since
  1-sample-per-condition confounds "chemical effect" with "which library," same
  root cause as the DEG issue below.

  Three real bugs found and fixed via testing against real data, not just code
  review:
  - The motivating bug itself: DESeq2 was silently defaulting to an alphabetical
  reference level for >2-condition data.
  - A factor-vs-character bug: obs[[condition]] comes back as an R factor via
  the h5ad/zellkonverter path, and passing a bare factor value to
  relevel(ref=...) either crashes or silently miscomputes — affected both
  run_deseq2()'s fallback path and run_milo(). Fixed with as.character() at
  three extraction points.
  - A Milo blank-PDF bug: plotDAbeeswarm() renders non-significant points
  invisibly (NA color), so 0 significant hits produced a
  technically-valid-but-blank PDF. Now skipped with a log message, matching the
  existing GSEA "skip and log why" convention.

  Verified via: hard-fail path (4-level condition, no control set → clean
  error), full pipeline run on plastics_test (scCODA succeeds; DEG/Milo
  correctly attempt all 3 real contrasts and gracefully report the same
  no-replicates limitation as before, now for the right reason), a synthetic
  3-condition/2-replicate dataset (confirms the success path writes
  correctly-named, correctly-computed tables), and two full runs on the existing
  2-level 5k_human_PBMC dataset (confirms no regression, and validates
  DEG+GSEA+Milo all succeed when there's real replication).

  envs/python_env.yaml and envs/r_env.yaml updated and the live conda envs
  already have the new packages installed. CLAUDE.md/README.md updated with the
  new contract. Nothing committed — happy to if you'd like.

