● Both changes fully implemented and verified end-to-end on real data:

  1. scDblFinder now runs in both modes. preprocess_qc.R needed zero changes (it
  already skipped SoupX gracefully and ran scDblFinder unconditionally). The
  fix was in run_pipeline.sh (Stage 1b now runs regardless of INPUT_MODE,
  writing matrix-mode output to a new PREPROCESS_QC_OUT directory —
  shared-across-projects, keyed-by-sample, following the same pattern as
  CELLRANGER_OUT rather than writing into your read-only MATRIX_DIR) and
  scanpy_analysis.py's load_samples() (new --preprocess-qc-dir arg to find
  doublet_calls.tsv in matrix mode). Verified on real plastics_test data:
  scDblFinder correctly flagged 32–100 doublets per sample, and load_samples()
  correctly merged them.

  2. New doublet visualization + optional removal:
  - 02c_doublet_summary.pdf (new figure) — doublet-score boxplots per sample,
  doublet fraction bar chart, and a UMAP colored by predicted_doublet. On real
  data this actually shows doublets clustering in specific UMAP regions rather
  than being randomly scattered — useful signal.
  - doublet_summary.tsv (new companion table) — per-sample cell/doublet counts.
  - REMOVE_DOUBLETS (new config flag, default false) — when true, drops flagged
  doublets during Stage 2 QC filtering, same place MAD-outliers are dropped.
  Verified: correctly removed exactly the 271 flagged cells, with
  doublet_summary.tsv showing 0 remaining afterward.

  Caught one real bug via testing: I'd used R's "grey70" color-naming convention
  for the muted/singlet color, but that's invalid in matplotlib — fixed to
  "0.7" (matplotlib's grayscale-float equivalent).

  All of CLAUDE.md, README.md, config.sh, and my_project.sh updated to document
  PREPROCESS_QC_OUT and REMOVE_DOUBLETS. Nothing committed.

