  Summary: Removed SAMPLES=() from config.sh/my_project.sh entirely.
  run_pipeline.sh now derives the sample list directly from METADATA_FILE's
  sample column (by header name, not position, so column order doesn't matter)
  right after config loads — before it's needed anywhere (Cell Ranger, Stage 1b,
  matrix verification, scanpy). Added two safety checks: it dies clearly if the
  sample column is missing, and if it contains duplicate values.

  This incidentally fixes a real, existing bug in your my_project.sh: it
  currently has METADATA_FILE pointing at 5k_human_pbmc.tsv but a leftover
  SAMPLES=() list still holding the old plastics_test sample names — exactly the
  kind of manual-sync drift this change eliminates. Verified against both real
  metadata files (5k_human_pbmc.tsv → correctly derives the 4 donor names;
  plastics.tsv → correctly derives the 4 condition names) and the error paths
  (missing column, duplicates), all via safe dry-runs that never triggered a
  real Cell Ranger invocation.

